  <div class="s-provenExperience">
    <div class="s-provenExperience__row">
      <p class="s-provenExperience__description">Smarter ingredient choices lead to safer products that work. But finding the best naturally derived and plant-derived ingredients isn’t easy. It requires an advanced knowledge of where to find better ingredients and how they work in advanced product formulations. We have been pioneers in this area for almost four decades.</p>
      <img src="//cdnsc1.melaleuca.com/na/images/product-store/ingredients-proven-experience.png" alt="Alt Text for image" class="s-provenExperience__img">
    </div>
    <ul class="s-provenExperience__list">
      <li class="s-provenExperience__item">
        <span role="text" class="s-provenExperience__text">
          <p class="leading-tight text-gray-120 text-sm w-full"><span class="font-bold text-green-150 uppercase">A safer and effective solution—Citric Acid.</span> To cheaply eliminate the appearance of hard water spots and soap scum, chlorine bleach is an easy choice. It works exceptionally well and is readily available. But it’s also extremely dangerous. We never use chlorine bleach. Citric acid is the smarter choice. It is naturally found in citrus fruits like lemons. It’s biodegradable, gentle on the environment, safer, and effective.</p>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="s-provenExperience__item">
        <span role="text" class="s-provenExperience__text">
          <p class="leading-tight text-gray-120 text-sm w-full"><span class="font-bold text-green-150 uppercase">Not all plant-derived ingredients are free from harmful effects.</span> Palm oil is a tricky natural ingredient. Unless obtained from a truly sustainable source, the extraction process actually causes significant harm to the important habitats where it is harvested due to widespread deforestation. In these cases, an organic compound (an ingredient from the ground rather than plants) may be the more responsible, smarter choice. When we do choose to use palm oil, it is only from a certified, renewable, environmentally sustainable source.</p>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="s-provenExperience__item">
        <span role="text" class="s-provenExperience__text">
          <p class="leading-tight text-gray-120 text-sm w-full"><span class="font-bold text-green-150 uppercase">Minimizing the amount of an ingredient used.</span> As of today, there are no effective plant-derived preservatives. If one were available, we would use it. In the meantime, we select the safest, most effective preservatives that allow us to use the tiniest amounts possible. We never use cheaper preservatives known to cause health issues such as formaldehyde or parabens.</p>
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="s-provenExperience__item">
        <span role="text" class="s-provenExperience__text">
          <p class="leading-tight text-gray-120 text-sm w-full"><span class="font-bold text-green-150 uppercase">Safely and effectively formulating our super-concentrated products.</span> We use a biodegradable surfactant, or cleaning agent, called TEA-LAS. It is extremely efficient at removing stains and oils from clothes. This organic compound has a proven track record of safety and because it is highly biodegradable, and it doesn’t have a negative impact on the environment. It allows us to safely and effectively formulate our super-concentrated products which saves plastic, fuel, and greenhouse gases.</p>
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>
